* The package's device names the GF180MCU decks lack, for ngspice (pdk_logic.Install.simulation_includes;
* Spectre reads the same definitions from spectre_devices.scs). Include after the models (the MOS
* corner and res_<corner>).

* the 3.3 V core pair by the package's names: the decks' nfet_03v3 / pfet_03v3 name both a
* subcircuit and model cards, which Spectre cannot bind by name (SFE-405); called here by X line
.subckt nfet_3v3 d g s b w=2.2e-7 l=2.8e-7 nf=1 m=1 ad=0 as=0 pd=0 ps=0
x0 d g s b nfet_03v3 w=w l=l nf=nf m=m ad=ad as=as pd=pd ps=ps
.ends nfet_3v3
.subckt pfet_3v3 d g s b w=2.2e-7 l=2.8e-7 nf=1 m=1 ad=0 as=0 pd=0 ps=0
x0 d g s b pfet_03v3 w=w l=l nf=nf m=m ad=ad as=as pd=pd ps=ps
.ends pfet_3v3

* the unsalicided P+ poly resistor by its body's length and width (meters), the parameters of
* frida's poly-resistor requests (flow/layout/devices/polyres), on the deck's ppolyf_u
.subckt ppolyf_u_lw p n b l=2e-6 w=8e-7
xr p n b ppolyf_u r_length=l r_width=w
.ends ppolyf_u_lw
